From 1c1afa0407f7e2444ee45dda4b865e0e2f5ac607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] _parse_extent_start_points(): bound the number of points by
 the data left

CVE-2026-112283. The extent start points extension of a ClipInfo file
(extension 2.4) declares num_point as a 32-bit value read from the file.
_parse_extent_start_points() passed it straight to calloc(num_point,
sizeof(uint32_t)) and then called bs_read(bits, 32) num_point times: up
to 16 GiB requested and about 4.3e9 iterations for a .clpi of a few
bytes, so a crafted disc, image or folder exhausts memory and CPU while
the clip is opened.

Each point takes 32 bits of the file. bs_avail() is the number of bits
between the read position and the end of the file, so a count larger
than bs_avail() / 32 cannot be stored in it. This is the bound
_parse_ep_map_stream() already applies to the EP coarse and fine tables
("unexpected EOF"), and with it the allocation is at most the size of
the file.

On failure num_point is set to 0 and nothing is allocated, like the
out-of-memory path above it. bdmv_parse_extension_data()
(extdata_parse.c) ignores the handler's return value and goes on with
the next extension entry, and _clpi_parse() goes on with ClipInfo,
sequence, program and CPI as before: only the extent start point list
is left empty. Nothing in libbluray reads cl->extent_start besides its
free in _clpi_free().

Not fixed in libbluray's master as of 448f89609163 (2026-10-09).
---
 src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c b/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c
index 29d0dbf..93a0818 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c
@@ -665,6 +665,12 @@ _parse_extent_start_points(BITSTREAM *bits, CLPI_EXTENT_START *es)
     bs_skip(bits, 32); // length
     es->num_point = bs_read(bits, 32);
 
+    if (bs_avail(bits)/(8*4) < es->num_point) {
+        BD_DEBUG(DBG_HDMV|DBG_CRIT, "clpi_parse: unexpected EOF (extent start points)\n");
+        es->num_point = 0;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     es->point = calloc(es->num_point, sizeof(uint32_t));
     if (es->num_point && !es->point) {
         es->num_point = 0;
-- 
